## Observations on Unauthenticated vs Authenticated Scanning

Running unauthenticated scans on both targets gives the attacker's perspective — what's visible from the network without any credentials. For Metasploitable this was devastating because the vulnerabilities are so severe they're detectable from outside.

For the Windows machine, an authenticated scan would go deeper. With credentials, Nessus can:
- Check Windows Update patch levels
- Enumerate installed software versions against CVE databases
- Check registry settings and local security policy
- Inspect running processes and services

That would likely surface more findings on the Windows machine. Something to explore in a follow-up scan.

